\begin{proof}
The estimate for any given $D_z$ is the content of [inf dets stab bdls...]. In particular, each constant $c_z$ is determined by the Riemannian geometry of $D_z$, as it comes essentially from an application of Sobolev's embedding theorem, hence it varies continuously with $z$. As $\left.\mathcal{E}\right\vert_{D}$ is itself an instance of our hypotheses, with metric $\left.H_0\right\vert_{D}$ over $D=D_0$, we have in this case $c_0>0$. Now one can certainly pick smaller $\delta>0,$ in \emph{Definition 12}, so that $\left\vert z\right\vert < \delta \Rightarrow c_z>\frac{c_0}{2}$, say.   
